<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle $116/dressed, flat-up $1-trade.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle $116/dressed, flat-up $1-trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska feedlot cattle markets near midday Wednesday were active, with sales at $115.00 to mostly $116.00 on a dressed basis, steady to up $1.00 from the bulk of Tuesday's sales, market sources said.</p>
<p>There were about 10,000 head sold, which would bring the week to date figure close to 45,000, the sources said.</p>
<p>This week's showlist was estimated near 53,000 head, they said. Feedlot cattle prices were supported by a light supply of unfinished cattle in the showlist and by moderately strong beef demand, the market sources said.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720--</p>
</text>
